 `experimental_page: "mobile"` mounts a plugin settings section exclusively on Settings → Mobile when that plugin owns the selected access provider, retaining plugin context, lifecycle, and error boundaries. Omission keeps the section on its plugin configuration page. Stabilization requires verifying placement isolation, plugin disable/uninstall, loading and failure states, and pairing lifecycle on Mobile.

+## `experimental_CompanionView` and `experimental_CompanionOutlet`
+
+An app-overlay owner keeps a companion component mounted while BB moves one
+persistent DOM container between its floating placeholder, a dynamic tab in
+the native right panel, and a matching main nav-panel outlet. Identity is
+scoped by plugin ID and companion ID. The portal keeps its React ownership,
+plugin CSS root, draft and attachment inputs, editor state, and scroll during
+placement and route changes. Increment `activation` for explicit focus;
+zero registers in the background. Metadata updates do not reverse dismissal
+or steal selection from native Browser/Terminal tabs. Pins participate in the
+native tab strip's close policy. Only the focused main pane hosts companions.
+The owner persists identities and placement; the host keeps native selection,
+tab order, dismissal, and activation baselines in per-window session storage.
+Removing the owner disposes its live view. The test runtime renders
+View children inline and has no native panel or main outlet implementation.
+
+Before stabilization:
+
+1. Verify real plugin views and SDK composers across floating, native panel,
+   main, route changes, native browser/terminal selection, and split panes.
+2. Exercise duplicate IDs, plugin unload/reload, explicit close, retained
+   attachments, focus, scroll, and editor state without portal remounts.
+3. Verify compact drawers and host resizing in Safari and desktop Chromium.
+4. Ship the suite's command/CLI placement controller and a released host
+   capability. Maintain stable SDK fallback until that host reaches stable.
+5. Confirm owner persistence, background activation, pinned tabs, tab reorder,
+   and dismissal restoration with real suite captures.
+
+
